            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for an exchange rate, then the Telugu for to dodge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కొలత",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొలత — kolata — \"a measurement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దర్జీ నా చొక్కా కొలతలు తీసుకున్నాడు. darjī nā cokkā kolatalu tīsukunnāḍu. The tailor took my measurements for a shirt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: కొలతలు, kolatalu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun of కొలుచు, to measure. కొలతలు తీసుకో, to take measurements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొలత (kolata) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1827 lists Telugu kolãta, \"measurement, measuring\", beside kolucu, \"to measure\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
